# Harness artefacts

Chat is ephemeral; these files are memory. One owner per artefact.

## Core paths

| Path | Owner | Purpose |
|------|-------|---------|
| `docs/project/project.md` | planner / human | Product truth, lifecycle stage, delivery requirements |
| `docs/project/roadmap.md` | planner | Phases → epics; **update every issue close** |
| `docs/project/eval-rubric.md` | planner | Global quality bar |
| `docs/project/setup.md` | human / generator | **CI commands**, MCPs, env vars |
| `docs/project/generator-state.md` | generator | Session handoff |
| `docs/project/issues/<n>/spec.md` | planner | Issue scope |
| `docs/project/issues/<n>/rubric.md` | planner | Issue done-criteria; lists required reviewers |
| `docs/project/feedback/<n>/` | reviewers + generator | See below |
| `docs/adr/NNNN-*.md` | architect → human accepts | Why decisions were made |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | generator | **Required for every S issue** |

Templates: `docs/project/templates/`

## Work sizing

Agent proposes S/M/L/XL; human confirms. **Always** GitHub issue + plan → generate → review.

| Size | Depth |
|------|-------|
| S | Light spec/rubric + CHANGELOG |
| M | Full spec + rubric |
| L | Multiple issues |
| XL | Phase 0 + staging (XL only) |

## Hybrid rubric

Reviewers read **both** `eval-rubric.md` and `issues/<n>/rubric.md`. Fail if either violated.

## Feedback naming

One folder per issue: `docs/project/feedback/<n>/`

- Reviewers: `<type>-i<iteration>.md` (e.g. `code-review-i1.md`)
- Generator only: `generator-response-i<iteration>.md`
- Never edit prior iteration files; add new files.

## ADRs

- **proposed** — not binding for implementation
- **accepted** — generator and reviewers must comply
- Link from issue spec `## Related ADRs` and PR body
- Skill: `.cursor/skills/architecture-decision-records/SKILL.md`

## CI profile

Canonical commands in `docs/project/setup.md`. Phase 3 testing gate and GitHub Actions must match.

## ADR vs project.md

| | project.md | ADR |
|--|------------|-----|
| What | Current stack summary | Why chosen, alternatives rejected |

If reversing the decision causes meaningful rework → ADR required.